{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfboz4CgNErnDAnQNSPYe", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's a regex for an ISO 8601 calendar date in `YYYY-MM-DD` form:\n\n```regex\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```\n\n- `\\d{4}` is a four-digit year.\n- `(0[1-9]|1[0-2])` is a month from 01 to 12.\n- `(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])` is a day from 01 to 31.\n- `^` and `$` make it match the whole string. Remove them if you want to find dates inside longer text, and use `\\b` instead.\n\nIt matches `2026-10-01` and rejects `2026-13-01` and `2026-10-32`.\n\nIt doesn't check the number of days in each month, so it would accept `2026-02-31`. If that matters, check the match with a date parser. In Python, for example, `datetime.date.fromisoformat(s)` raises an error for dates that don't exist."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 631, "cache_read_input_tokens": 23988, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 631}, "output_tokens": 320, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "92d46520-26ed-4a1b-bf7f-953cc446c285", "uuid": "746225da-0e42-4341-93c7-037cd1139f7d", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T16:11:48.055Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfboz3cTJhykzbr7vAHar"}
